      "created_at": "2025-02-26T19:14:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-02-26T19:14:17Z",
      "body": "We should detach the object from the dictionary when the object is freed (which should involve copying the values and assigning a new values). \n\nSo couldn't we check in the clear loop if the values have changed from `oldvalues` and if so then start over with the new `oldvalues`? Maybe only do that once in the embedded case as there's probably also recursion issues where clearing inserts into the dictionary and causes it to resize :P",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
